---
title: JavaScript API Wrapper
description: Use the JavaScript wrapper for easier, more reliable API calls from themes and modules.
---

{% aside type="note" %}
If you're building themes or modules, use this wrapper instead of making raw browser API calls. It handles CSRF tokens, response parsing, and other repetitive details for you.
{% /aside %}

## Why Use the Wrapper?

- **Automatic CSRF handling** — No need to manage tokens manually
- **Built-in spinner** — Shows a loading indicator during requests
- **Less coupling** — If the API changes, the wrapper absorbs more of that churn
- **Cleaner code** — Less boilerplate for you

## Importing the Wrapper

The bundled admin and Huraga themes already load the wrapper. For a custom theme, add this to your base layout before your theme JavaScript:

```twig
{{ 'js/fossbilling.js'|public_asset_url|script_tag }}
{{ 'js/api.js'|public_asset_url|script_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'build/js/mytheme.js'|asset_url }}"></script>
```

The `script_tag` filter adds a cache-busting hash and prevents the same script from being rendered more than once.

The wrapper automatically binds API forms and links when the page loads.

## CSRF Tokens

Load a FOSSBilling page first to establish the session and token. The wrapper reads the `fossbilling_csrf` cookie and sends the token on same-origin requests, including protected guest calls. If you include a `CSRFToken` form field explicitly, use the current page’s token. See the [API reference](/extensions-and-development/api/#csrf-tokens) for which requests require a token and where to send it.

## Making Requests

The wrapper follows this pattern:

```text
FOSSBilling.api.{role}.{method}(endpoint, params, onSuccess, onError, showSpinner)
```

| Parameter | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| `role` | `admin`, `client`, or `guest` |
| `method` | Use `get` or `post` for core routes; guest authentication requires `post`. Prefer `post` for mutations. |
| `endpoint` | The API endpoint (e.g., `"currency/get_pairs"`) |
| `params` | Request parameters (object) |
| `onSuccess` | Callback that receives the API response's `result` value. |
| `onError` | Callback that receives `{ message, code }` when the request fails. |
| `showSpinner` | Boolean to show/hide the loading spinner (optional, default: `true`) |

## Examples

### Get Currency Pairs (Guest)

```javascript
FOSSBilling.api.guest.get(
  "currency/get_pairs",
  {},
  function(response) {
    console.log("Currency pairs:", response);
  },
  function(error) {
    console.error("Error:", error);
  }
);
```

### Get Client List (Admin)

```javascript
FOSSBilling.api.admin.post(
  "client/get_list",
  { per_page: 10, page: 1 },
  function(response) {
    console.log("Clients:", response.list);
  },
  function(error) {
    console.error("Failed to load clients:", error);
  }
);
```

## Loading Spinner

The wrapper creates and removes the spinner element automatically. Your theme provides the `.spinner-border` styling.

![Spinner example](../../../assets/docs/spinner-example.gif)

Pass `false` as the fifth argument to disable the spinner for a request:

```javascript
FOSSBilling.api.admin.post('client/get_list', {}, onSuccess, onError, false);
```

## API Forms and Links

The Twig helpers `fb_api_form()` and `fb_api_link()` render a `data-fb-api` attribute that the wrapper uses for automatic form and link handling.

Use `api_url` for the target endpoint:

```twig
<form action="{{ 'profile/update'|api_url }}" {{ fb_api_form({ message: 'Profile updated'|trans }) }}>
  <input type="text" name="first_name" value="{{ profile.first_name }}">
  <button type="submit">{{ 'Save'|trans }}</button>
</form>
```

`fb_api_form()` adds `method="post"` and `data-fb-api`. The wrapper serializes the form, adds the CSRF token automatically for session-authenticated calls, disables enabled buttons while the request is running, and shows errors with `FOSSBilling.message()`.

For API links:

```twig
<a href="{{ 'client/delete'|api_url(query: { id: client.id }, role: 'admin') }}"
   {{ fb_api_link({
     modal: { type: 'confirm', title: 'Are you sure?'|trans },
     redirect: 'client'|url
   }) }}>
  {{ 'Delete'|trans }}
</a>
```

The wrapper intercepts links with `data-fb-api`, sends a `GET` request to the link `href`, and then handles the configured follow-up action.

Supported `data-fb-api` options:

| Option | Applies to | Description |
|--------|------------|-------------|
| `message` | Forms and links | Show a success toast after the request. |
| `redirect` | Forms and links | Redirect to the given URL after success. |
| `reload` | Forms and links | Pass `true` to reload the current page after success. |
| `callback` | Forms and links | Name of a global `window` function to call with the API result. |
| `params` | Links | Extra request parameters merged into the link request. |
| `modal` | Links | Show a confirmation, danger, or prompt modal before the request. |

Prompt modals require a `key`; the entered value is sent under that request parameter name:

```twig
<a href="{{ 'example/update_name'|api_url }}"
   {{ fb_api_link({
     modal: { type: 'prompt', title: 'New name'|trans, label: 'Name'|trans, key: 'name' },
     reload: true
   }) }}>
  {{ 'Rename'|trans }}
</a>
```

## Manual Requests

If you need to call the API without the wrapper, see the [`fetch()` example in the API reference](/extensions-and-development/api/#manual-browser-requests).

## Complete Example

```javascript
function loadProfile() {
  FOSSBilling.api.client.get(
    "profile/get",
    {},
    function(profile) {
      document.getElementById('name').textContent = profile.first_name + ' ' + profile.last_name;
      document.getElementById('email').textContent = profile.email;
    },
    function(error) {
      alert('Failed to load profile: ' + error.message);
    }
  );
}

document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', loadProfile);
```

For more details, see the [API Reference](/extensions-and-development/api/).
